# ABOUTME: Phones allowed to reach acm bridge on this server (public keys only)
# ABOUTME: scripts/setup-acm-fleet.sh installs these lines into ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
#
# One line per phone, exactly as `acm mobile key-line` prints it. Run it on the server,
# passing --acm so the forced command survives garbage collection:
#
#   acm mobile key-line --acm "$HOME/.nix-profile/bin/acm" --level p3 --name pixel-10-pro <pubkey-file>
#
# which gives:
#
#   command="/home/fx/.nix-profile/bin/acm bridge --allow p3",restrict ecdsa-sha2-nistp256 AAAA... pixel-10-pro
#
# Any other form of line is refused.
#
# Revoke a phone by removing its line by merge request, then on the server run
# dev-update, scripts/setup-acm-fleet.sh and scripts/install-ntfy.sh, in that order:
# the scripts read the server's clone and do not update it. An edit made in the
# clone is reset away. For a revocation that cannot wait, see "Revoking a phone"
# in the README.
#
# To keep the keys out of the repository, use ~/.config/acm/phone-keys.pub on the
# server instead (it wins over this file), or point ACM_PHONE_KEYS_FILE at a file.
